course: dictionary
lesson: 14101
title: Menstruation: a normal part of growing up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Menstruation is a long word for something natural and healthy. It means the monthly bleeding from the womb that happens to girls and women. Many people call it «having a period».
explain: «Menstruation usually starts when a girl is between about 8 and 16 years old.» Look at the clues: it happens every month, and it is part of growing up. It is a normal body process, not an illness.
explain: «Many women use pads, tampons or menstrual cups during menstruation.» The sentence tells you that people use products to manage it. Schools in many places give period products for free, so nobody has to feel alone or worried about it.
fact: Menstruation means the natural monthly bleeding from the womb.
fact: It usually starts at puberty, often between the ages of 8 and 16, and usually continues until about age 50.
fact: «Having a period» is another everyday name for menstruation.
fact: Menstruation is a normal part of growing up, and it is nothing to be ashamed of.
fact: Pads, tampons, period pants and menstrual cups are some of the products people use during menstruation.
exercise: «Menstruation is a natural part of growing up.» What does menstruation mean? | A type of fever | A kind of exercise | A sort of sweet food | * The natural monthly bleeding from the womb
exercise: Which everyday phrase is another name for menstruation? | Having a birthday | Having a bath | * Having a period | Having a nap
exercise: «Pads, tampons and menstrual cups are period products.» Which of these is a period product? | Toothbrush | Football | Tiger | * Menstrual cup
test: «Menstruation usually begins at puberty.» What is puberty? | The name of a dance | A holiday in the mountains | * The time when the body starts changing as a child grows up | A type of school trip
test: Why does the lesson say menstruation is normal? | It is a sign of a broken bone | It only happens once in a lifetime | * It is a natural part of growing up | It means the body is ill
exam: Which sentence about menstruation is true? | It is an illness that needs medicine every single day | It only happens to boys | * It usually begins around puberty, between about 8 and 16 | It happens just once in a whole life and never again
